-- A rejected member occurrence authored as a property access (no parentheses and no
-- argument list) must consume its own member token and keep the enclosing body parsable,
-- so the later independent `render_count(count)` use still registers `count`'s exact U64
-- receiver before the delayed ordinary diagnostic is issued.
--
-- The whole `4_294_967_296` does not fit I32, so a name-consumption path that stopped on
-- the member symbol, or that skipped the following statement, would report the literal's
-- range or the defaulted receiver instead of the unknown-member diagnostic on U64.

render_count |value U64| -> String:
    return cast value
;

count = 4_294_967_296
result = count.unsupported
render_count(count)

[:unreachable]
